.TH PAKMAN.PY 1 "2026-09-12" "3.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
PakMan.py \- a graphical, fast, careful Python package updater
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 PakMan.py
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B PakMan.py
upgrades the outdated Python packages of the interpreter that runs it. It
renders the outdated list as a box\-drawn table, attempts a single batch
resolver run before falling back to isolated per\-package upgrades, writes a
rollback snapshot first, distinguishes dependency conflicts it introduced from
ones that were already there, refuses to run twice at once, and audits every
subprocess to
.I ~/.pakman.log\c
\&.
.PP
To update a virtual environment, invoke PakMan with that environment's
interpreter:
.RS
.EX
~/projects/api/.venv/bin/python PakMan.py -y
.EE
.RE
.PP
Column arithmetic is done in terminal columns rather than characters: emoji and
CJK text are double\-width, while combining marks, variation selectors and
joiners take no space at all. Borders line up whatever a package name contains,
and truncation never splits a double\-width character in half.
.PP
All presentation degrades on its own. A non\-TTY output stream, the
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable,
.B TERM=dumb
or a non\-UTF\-8 stream independently drop color, the live progress line, or
box\-drawing characters; the content is never lost.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Selection
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Auto-approve all upgrades without an interactive prompt.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-interactive .
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Show a numbered table and choose which packages to upgrade. Accepts
selections like
.BR 1,3,5\-7 ,
.BR all ,
or
.BR none .
Selection implies consent; no second confirmation prompt is shown.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " PKG " [ PKG " ...]"
Packages to skip. Case-insensitive glob patterns are supported:
.RS
.EX
python3 PakMan.py --exclude 'boto*' numpy
.EE
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-only " PKG " [ PKG " ...]"
Upgrade only packages matching these names or globs, case-insensitively. A name
may not appear in both
.B \-\-only
and
.BR \-\-exclude .
.SS Behaviour
.TP
.B \-\-check\-only
List outdated packages and exit without upgrading. Exits with status 3 if any
were found.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print every command that would be executed without running any of them.
Skips the confirmation prompt and the instance lock.
.TP
.B \-\-upgrade\-pip
Upgrade pip itself before upgrading packages. A failure here is reported and
the run continues; the pip already installed can still do the work.
.TP
.B \-\-pre
Include pre-release versions when upgrading.
.TP
.B \-\-only\-binary
Refuse source distributions by passing
.B \-\-only\-binary=:all:
to the installer, so no sdist build code executes.
.TP
.B \-\-require\-venv
Refuse to run outside a virtual environment (exit 1). Without it, running
against a global interpreter prints a warning naming the interpreter, plus a
further warning if the interpreter is marked externally managed (PEP 668).
.TP
.B \-\-audit
Run
.B pip-audit
after upgrading. Its absence is detected with
.B pip show
and reported, not treated as a failure.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-rollback
Skip writing the rollback snapshot file.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-batch
Skip the batch upgrade attempt and go straight to per-package upgrades.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-lock
Allow concurrent runs by skipping the single-instance lock.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
Ignore
.IR ~/.pakmanrc.json .
.TP
.BI \-\-export " FILE"
Run
.B pip freeze
after upgrading and write the result to FILE.
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Send a native macOS notification (via
.BR osascript )
when the run completes. Notification text is escaped to prevent AppleScript
injection.
.SS Performance
.TP
.B \-\-uv
Use
.B uv
for the installs as well as the outdated check. Typically several times faster
than pip. Requires uv on PATH; if it is missing, PakMan warns and uses pip.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-uv
Do not use uv at all, even if it is installed. By default uv is used for the
outdated check whenever it is present.
.TP
.BI \-\-jobs " N"
Number of parallel wheel-prefetch workers, 1 to 16. Default is
.BR 6 .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-prefetch
Do not pre-download wheels in parallel.
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " N"
Number of attempts per package before it is marked failed. Retries use
exponential backoff. Default is
.BR 2 ,
minimum is
.BR 1 .
Errors that cannot succeed on a retry are never retried.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECS"
Timeout per package in seconds; the batch attempt is allowed this many seconds
times the package count. Default is
.BR 600 .
.SS Output
.TP
.BI \-\-color " auto|always|never"
Force or suppress ANSI color. Default
.B auto
respects
.BR NO_COLOR ,
.BR TERM=dumb ,
and whether stdout is a terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
ASCII-only output: no box-drawing characters and no emoji.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only warnings and errors. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-interactive .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Stream raw pip output instead of progress indicators.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the outdated package list as JSON to stdout and exit without upgrading.
.TP
.B \-\-summary\-json
Print a machine-readable summary of the completed run to stdout. Distinct from
.BR \-\-json ,
which reports what is outdated and exits. Both move the human-readable UI to
stderr so stdout stays parseable.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-json
Append one structured JSON record per run (upgraded, failures, excluded,
conflicts, new conflicts, rollback path, installer, elapsed, exit code) to
.IR ~/.pakman_history.jsonl .
The file is trimmed to the newest 500 records.
.TP
.BI \-\-history " [N]"
Print the last N recorded runs as a table and exit. Default is
.BR 15 .
.TP
.B \-\-rollbacks
List the rollback snapshots on disk, newest first, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success — nothing to do, or all upgrades succeeded. A run that introduces new
dependency conflicts still exits 0: no package failed. The conflicts are
reported in the summary, the log, and the JSON record.
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error (non-interactive session without \-y,
.B \-\-require\-venv
outside a venv, another run holds the lock, the outdated list could not be
read).
.TP
.B 2
Run completed but one or more packages failed.
.TP
.B 3
.B \-\-check\-only
found outdated packages.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with Ctrl-C or SIGTERM.
.SH FEATURES
.SS New versus Pre-existing Conflicts
A
.B pip check
baseline is taken before the upgrades — concurrently with the outdated query,
so it costs nothing — and compared against a
.B pip check
afterwards. Only conflicts the run introduced are reported as such, with a
pointer to the rollback file that undoes them; pre-existing conflicts the run
happened to resolve are reported separately.
.SS Batch Upgrade with Per-Package Fallback
Everything is first attempted in one resolver run, which is dramatically faster
than N runs and the only way the resolver can satisfy packages that constrain
each other. If the batch fails, each package is upgraded individually so a
single bad package cannot block the rest.
.SS Pipelined Parallel Prefetch
On the per-package path, wheels download on a thread pool while installs run.
Downloads are submitted in install order and the install loop waits only on the
package it is about to install, so the download of package N+1 overlaps the
installation of package N. Skipped under
.B \-\-uv
because uv resolves and downloads in parallel already.
.SS Single-Instance Lock
An flock on
.I ~/.pakman.lock
refuses to start a second run while one is in progress: two pip processes
writing the same site-packages is the classic way to end up with a
half-installed distribution. If the lock file cannot be created at all, the run
continues with a warning rather than refusing.
.SS Rollback Snapshots
Current versions are pinned to
.I ~/.pakman_rollback_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.txt
before anything is upgraded. Undo a run with
.BR "pip install -r <file>" ;
.B \-\-rollbacks
lists what is available.
.SS Security Hardening
Package names are validated against PEP 508 naming rules before reaching any
subprocess. Log, history, lock and rollback files are created mode 0600, and
the log rotates at 2 MB keeping 3 generations. Subprocesses inherit no stdin
and run with
.BR PIP_NO_INPUT=1 ,
so pip never stops to ask a question there is nothing to answer with. Every
subprocess call writes an AUDIT line with the exact shell-quoted command, exit
code, and duration to the log.
.SS Clean Interrupts and Cron Safety
Ctrl-C or SIGTERM mid-upgrade prints how many packages were upgraded, failed,
and not attempted, cancels pending downloads, then exits 130. In a non-TTY
session without
.BR \-y ,
the tool exits 1 immediately instead of hanging on the prompt.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I ~/.pakmanrc.json
supplies defaults for any of
.BR exclude ", " only ", " pre ", " only_binary ", " require_venv ", " audit ,
.BR no_uv ", " uv ", " no_rollback ", " no_batch ", " notify ", " jobs ,
.BR retries ", " timeout ", " log_json ", " color ", " ascii ", and " export .
Command-line flags override it; unknown or mistyped keys warn and are ignored.
.PP
.EX
{
  "exclude": ["boto*", "awscli"],
  "uv": true,
  "log_json": true
}
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Interactive upgrade (default):
.EX
python3 PakMan.py
.EE
.TP
Pick packages from a numbered table:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py -i
.EE
.TP
Auto-approve, skip all boto packages, notify:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py -y --exclude 'boto*' --notify
.EE
.TP
Let uv do the installs as well as the outdated check:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py -y --uv
.EE
.TP
Preview outdated packages (exit 3 if any found):
.EX
python3 PakMan.py --check-only
.EE
.TP
Update a specific virtualenv:
.EX
~/projects/api/.venv/bin/python PakMan.py -y
.EE
.TP
Refuse to touch anything outside a venv, and refuse source builds:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py --require-venv --only-binary -y
.EE
.TP
Upgrade, then audit and export a freeze:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py -y --audit --export requirements.lock
.EE
.TP
Cron-friendly run with JSON history:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py -y -q --log-json
.EE
.TP
Feed the outdated list to another tool:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py --json | jq -r '.[].name'
.EE
.TP
Feed the run result to another tool:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py -y --summary-json | jq '.new_conflicts'
.EE
.TP
Review recent runs and available rollbacks:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py --history 30
python3 PakMan.py --rollbacks
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.pakman.log
Timestamped log of all runs with per-command AUDIT lines. Mode 0600, rotated
at 2 MB with 3 generations kept.
.TP
.I ~/.pakman_history.jsonl
One JSON record per run when
.B \-\-log\-json
is set, trimmed to the newest 500. Mode 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.pakman.lock
Single-instance lock held for the duration of a run. Mode 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.pakmanrc.json
Optional defaults for command-line flags.
.TP
.I ~/.pakman_rollback_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.txt
Version snapshot written before upgrading; the five newest are kept. Restore
with
.BR "pip install -r <file>" .
Mode 0600.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, disables color under
.BR "\-\-color auto" .
.TP
.B TERM
.B dumb
or unset disables color and the live progress line under
.BR "\-\-color auto" .
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3.10 or later (standard library only) with pip available as
.BR "python -m pip" .
.PP
.B uv
(\fIhttps://github.com/astral\-sh/uv\fR) is optional: used for the outdated
check when present, and for installs with
.BR \-\-uv .
.B pip-audit
is optional, for
.BR \-\-audit .
The
.B \-\-notify
flag requires
.B osascript
(available by default on macOS).
.SH AUTHOR
Anirban Bagchi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pip (1),
